This PR fixes: #35292

`updateAvatar` and `setAvatarFromUrl` in `LiveContext` were empty stubs — any avatar set during a session was silently discarded. `customAvatar` state also initialized to `null` on every launch with no load-from-storage logic.

## Changes

- **`LiveContext.tsx`**
  - `customAvatar` state now lazy-initializes from `localStorage` (`mossy_custom_avatar` key)
  - `updateAvatar(file)` — reads file via `FileReader`, canvas-resizes to ≤512px, encodes as JPEG (0.85 quality), writes to `localStorage` + state
  - `setAvatarFromUrl(url)` — validates URL is `https://` or `data:image/` before persisting; rejects anything else to prevent arbitrary localStorage injection
  - `clearAvatar()` — now also removes the `localStorage` key

- **`resources/public/mossy-avatar.png`** — synced to match `src/renderer/src/assets/mossy-avatar.png`; the two copies had diverged (different MD5s), which would surface as the wrong default avatar image in packaged builds

```ts
// Before
const updateAvatar = async (file: File) => { };
const setAvatarFromUrl = async (url: string) => { };
const clearAvatar = () => setCustomAvatar(null);

// After
const updateAvatar = async (file: File) => {
  // FileReader → canvas resize → JPEG → localStorage + setState
};
const setAvatarFromUrl = async (url: string) => {
  if (!isDataUrl && !isHttpsUrl) return; // validated
  localStorage.setItem(AVATAR_STORAGE_KEY, url);
  setCustomAvatar(url);
};
const clearAvatar = () => {
  localStorage.removeItem(AVATAR_STORAGE_KEY);
  setCustomAvatar(null);
};
```

## Summary by Sourcery

Persist custom avatars across app restarts and ensure the correct default avatar asset is used in packaged builds.

New Features:
- Allow users to set a custom avatar that is persisted in localStorage and restored on app launch.

Bug Fixes:
- Prevent custom avatars from being lost on app restart by wiring avatar update, URL-setting, and clearing logic to state and localStorage.
- Align the public mossy avatar image with the renderer asset so packaged builds show the correct default avatar.

Enhancements:
- Validate external avatar URLs to only accept HTTPS and data image URLs before persisting them.
